  "duration_seconds": 305.131,
  "duration_after_vad_seconds": 302.651,
  "cue_count": 91,
  "cues": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 0.18,
      "end": 5.46,
      "text": "This is The Guardian's Guide to Scottish Independence for the non-Britains.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.187134,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037689
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 5.46,
      "end": 10.62,
      "text": "It's a long and complex story, but let's begin by answering the most fundamental question.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.187134,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037689
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 10.62,
      "end": 12.5,
      "text": "Where is Scotland anyway?",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.187134,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037689
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 12.5,
      "end": 15.9,
      "text": "The country of Scotland is right here, at the top of the island of Great Britain,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.187134,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037689
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 15.9,
      "end": 19.46,
      "text": "the crazy hat worn by the bearded troll who appears to be looking west,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.187134,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037689
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 19.46,
      "end": 22.02,
      "text": "toward Ireland, and laughing.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.187134,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037689
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 22.02,
      "end": 25.66,
      "text": "On Thursday the 18th of September, the people of Scotland will vote to decide",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.187134,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037689
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 25.66,
      "end": 28.82,
      "text": "whether or not it will become a country in its own right.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.187134,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037689
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 28.82,
      "end": 32.18,
      "text": "But wait, I hear you ask, didn't you just call Scotland a country?",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.119625,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.011322
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 32.18,
      "end": 34.66,
      "text": "Isn't Scotland already a country?",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.119625,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.011322
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 34.66,
      "end": 37.9,
      "text": "The definitive answer to that question is sort of.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.119625,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.011322
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 37.9,
      "end": 42.42,
      "text": "Technically, Scotland is a country within a country known as the United Kingdom.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.119625,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.011322
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 42.42,
      "end": 46.98,
      "text": "Scotland may have its own church, its own legal system, its own professional soccer league,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.119625,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.011322
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 46.98,
      "end": 50.62,
      "text": "and its own dietary idiosyncrasies, but it's still part of the UK,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.119625,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.011322
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 50.62,
      "end": 54.94,
      "text": "which also includes the countries of England, Wales, and Northern Ireland.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.119625,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.011322
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 54.94,
      "end": 58.02,
      "text": "Scottish people have British passports.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.119625,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.011322
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 58.02,
      "end": 62.66,
      "text": "Scotland did used to be a separate country, with its own king, James VI.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13365,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037262
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 62.66,
      "end": 68.5,
      "text": "Then in 1603, Queen Elizabeth, not that one, this one, died without leaving an heir,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13365,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037262
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 68.5,
      "end": 72.1,
      "text": "and the nearest relative they could find turned out to be her cousin James.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13365,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037262
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 72.1,
      "end": 77.74,
      "text": "He became James I of England, while still keeping his job as James VI of Scotland.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13365,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037262
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 77.74,
      "end": 80.34,
      "text": "If you think that's confusing, you ain't heard nothing yet.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13365,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037262
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 80.34,
      "end": 84.02,
      "text": "England and Scotland maintained a monarch sharing arrangement for over a century,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13365,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.037262
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 84.02,
      "end": 88.26,
      "text": "before the Acts of the Union in 1707 made the two nations a single entity,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.149816,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.205811
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 88.26,
      "end": 90.98,
      "text": "with one parliament located in London.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.149816,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.205811
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 90.98,
      "end": 93.78,
      "text": "Scotland went along with this largely because it was almost bankrupt,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.149816,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.205811
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 93.78,
      "end": 98.02,
      "text": "thanks to something called the Darien disaster, which happened way over here,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.149816,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.205811
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 98.02,
      "end": 101.5,
      "text": "and is, frankly, another story for another time.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.149816,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.205811
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 101.5,
      "end": 108.48,
      "text": "Let's have a stirring musical interlude before we skip ahead, way ahead.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.149816,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.205811
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 108.48,
      "end": 111.28,
      "text": "In the 1970s, speculation about devolution,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.149816,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.205811
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 111.28,
      "end": 114.44,
      "text": "the notion of returning a measure of power to a Scottish government,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.149816,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.205811
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 114.44,
      "end": 118.0,
      "text": "gave rise to what used to be known as the West Lothian Question.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.115279,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.087097
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 118.0,
      "end": 121.4,
      "text": "For most people in the UK today, the real West Lothian Question is,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.115279,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.087097
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 121.4,
      "end": 124.04,
      "text": "what is the West Lothian Question?",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.115279,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.087097
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 124.04,
      "end": 129.48,
      "text": "The West Lothian Question was named after the Scottish constituency of the MP who first asked it.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.115279,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.087097
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 129.48,
      "end": 134.4,
      "text": "To paraphrase, he basically posited a world where Scotland had its own regional parliament,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.115279,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.087097
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 134.4,
      "end": 138.4,
      "text": "but also continued to send representatives to the British parliament in London.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.115279,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.087097
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 138.4,
      "end": 142.96,
      "text": "How could it be, he asked, that Scottish MPs could vote on laws that affected only England,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.115279,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.087097
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 142.96,
      "end": 145.72,
      "text": "and yet had no vote on matters that affected Scotland?",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.133387,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.004971
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 145.72,
      "end": 147.92,
      "text": "That would be totally crazy.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.133387,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.004971
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 147.92,
      "end": 150.48,
      "text": "You weren't really meant to answer the West Lothian Question,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.133387,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.004971
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 150.48,
      "end": 154.12,
      "text": "it was just there to demonstrate that a Scottish parliament couldn't logically exist,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.133387,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.004971
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 154.12,
      "end": 157.04,
      "text": "and that if you tried to set one up, the universe would disappear.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.133387,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.004971
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 157.04,
      "end": 159.68,
      "text": "Or something.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.133387,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.004971
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 159.68,
      "end": 163.2,
      "text": "After a referendum on devolution, they did set up a Scottish parliament,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.133387,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.004971
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 163.2,
      "end": 165.52,
      "text": "with its very own brand new building.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.133387,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.004971
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 165.52,
      "end": 168.48,
      "text": "I know, but it's meant to be really nice on the inside.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.133387,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.004971
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 168.48,
      "end": 171.28,
      "text": "Devolution is not the same as being a separate country.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.133387,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.004971
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 171.28,
      "end": 174.4,
      "text": "The British parliament merely outsourced certain powers to Scotland,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13985,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.058929
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 174.4,
      "end": 175.84,
      "text": "rather than handing them over,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13985,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.058929
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 175.84,
      "end": 180.04,
      "text": "and it reserved the right to overturn any law made in the Scottish legislation.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13985,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.058929
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 180.04,
      "end": 182.88,
      "text": "In 2011, the Scottish National Party,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13985,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.058929
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 182.88,
      "end": 186.44,
      "text": "a party that campaigned on a pledge to hold an independence referendum,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13985,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.058929
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 186.44,
      "end": 189.0,
      "text": "won a landslide in the Scottish parliament.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13985,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.058929
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 189.0,
      "end": 192.36,
      "text": "The SNP leader, this man, Alex Salmon,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13985,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.058929
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 192.36,
      "end": 194.56,
      "text": "you don't pronounce the L like with a fish,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13985,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.058929
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 194.56,
      "end": 199.04,
      "text": "became Scotland's first minister and promised a referendum within the election cycle.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.13985,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.058929
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 199.04,
      "end": 203.12,
      "text": "In 2012, British Prime Minister David Cameron finally agreed to a referendum,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144717,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.003426
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 203.12,
      "end": 203.88,
      "text": "saying,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144717,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.003426
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 203.88,
      "end": 208.32,
      "text": "this United Kingdom can never hold a country within it, without its consent.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144717,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.003426
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 208.32,
      "end": 209.6,
      "text": "What he meant was,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144717,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.003426
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 209.6,
      "end": 212.68,
      "text": "I'm allowing this because it's certain to fail.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144717,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.003426
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 212.68,
      "end": 217.24,
      "text": "Polls consistently show that only a minority of Scots would vote for actual independence.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144717,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.003426
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 217.24,
      "end": 219.92,
      "text": "A yes campaign was set up, and also a no campaign,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144717,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.003426
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 219.92,
      "end": 223.28,
      "text": "which isn't called the no campaign, because that would sound a bit negative.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144717,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.003426
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 223.28,
      "end": 226.64,
      "text": "Instead, it's called Better Together, which is arguably worse.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144717,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.003426
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 226.64,
      "end": 229.72,
      "text": "Those in the yes camp include Alex Salmon and the SNP,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144896,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.036621
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 229.72,
      "end": 232.72,
      "text": "and also the Scottish Green Party, the Scottish Socialist Party,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144896,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.036621
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 232.72,
      "end": 236.88,
      "text": "possibly Rupert Murdoch, Sir Sean Connery, and both of the proclamers.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144896,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.036621
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 236.88,
      "end": 240.16,
      "text": "The no camp includes all three main political parties,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144896,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.036621
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 240.16,
      "end": 243.92,
      "text": "Harry Potter author J.K. Rowling, Susan Boyle, and one of the Doctor Who's,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144896,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.036621
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 243.92,
      "end": 246.64,
      "text": "not to mention a majority of the people in the rest of the UK,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144896,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.036621
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 246.64,
      "end": 249.28,
      "text": "who don't count because they don't get to vote.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144896,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.036621
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 249.28,
      "end": 252.68,
      "text": "Those conspicuously offering no opinion include Andy Murray,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144896,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.036621
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 252.68,
      "end": 255.0,
      "text": "Billy Connelly, and the Queen.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.144896,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.036621
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 255.0,
      "end": 258.24,
      "text": "Recently, the no camp's comfortable lead has eroded,",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.114187,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.009842
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 258.24,
      "end": 261.44,
      "text": "and a lot of questions that nobody had ever answered satisfactorily",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.114187,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.009842
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 261.44,
      "end": 263.64,
      "text": "have suddenly become interesting to people.",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.114187,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.009842
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 263.64,
      "end": 267.96,
      "text": "Questions like, if it were independent, what would Scotland use for money?",
      "source": "faster_whisper_small",
      "avg_logprob": -0.114187,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.009842
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 267.96,
